Optimal Solution - Count character frequencies and compute the difference between the largest odd frequency and smallest even frequency.
                   “Since only lowercase letters exist, I use a fixed 26-size frequency array, then greedily track the maximum odd and minimum even counts in one pass.”

class Solution {
    public int maxDifference(String s) {
        int n = s.length(); // Length of string
        int[] freq = new int[26]; // Frequency array for lowercase letters
        // Count frequency of each character
        for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) {
            freq[ch - 'a']++; // Map 'a' → 0, 'b' → 1 ... 'z' → 25
        }
        int maxOdd = 0; // Stores maximum odd frequency
        int minEven = n + 1; // Stores minimum even frequency (initialized large)
        // Traverse frequency array
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (freq[i] == 0)
                continue; // Skip characters not present
            // If frequency is even
            if (freq[i] % 2 == 0) {
                minEven = Math.min(minEven, freq[i]);
            }
            // If frequency is odd
            else {
                maxOdd = Math.max(maxOdd, freq[i]);
            }
        }
        // Return difference
        return maxOdd - minEven;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
